dialogue cohesion_generic_same_faction
title: The same banner
trigger: Cohesion faction:same faction:same level=2
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker with $with
speaker hero $hero

node open commander
  Two of the caravan's heroes have pulled their bedrolls close tonight. They grew up under the same banner, and it shows in small ways: the same knot in a boot lace, the same way of banking a fire.
  -> fire

node fire with
  You bank it the way we did back home. Ash on the windward side, so the wind can't get under it. I haven't seen anyone do that in years.
  -> others

node others hero
  Nobody else here does it right. I fix the others' fires when they aren't looking.
  -> strange

node strange with
  Commander, we came from the same place and never once met there. You'd think we'd have crossed paths a hundred times.
  * Home's big. You found each other out here. That's what counts. -> found
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 6
  * Then trade it back and forth. The streets, the songs, the people. -> share
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 8
  * Old loyalties get in the way on the road. Don't lean on them. -> road
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero -3

node found hero
  Out past every map we grew up with. Aye. That's something.
  -> square

node share hero
  Start with the bakery by the gate, then. If you knew the bakery, you knew everyone.
  -> square

node road with
  We won't lean. But we'll still bank the fire the right way.
  -> square

node square with
  The collectors came through twice a year. I always wondered who else stood in the square while they read the names out.
  -> stood

node stood hero
  I did. Every time. We might have stood a shoulder apart and never known it.
  * Next time a collector reads a name, you'll stand together on purpose. -> together
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 8
  * That square is behind you both now. -> behind
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 4
  * Some memories are better left in the square. -> leave
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero -2

node together with
  On purpose. Aye. Shoulder to shoulder, and loud about it.
  -> close

node behind hero
  Behind us. It doesn't feel like it some nights. Tonight it does.
  -> close

node leave with
  Left, then. Pass the salt, and we'll talk about something lighter.
  -> close

node close commander
  The two of them fall to arguing over the name of a hill outside home, and neither will give it up, and both are smiling.
